WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.313
It's one of those

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.440
"Did I really see that?"

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.268
TV moments in season eight, episode three

00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:18.300
of "Game of Thrones."

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.270
We see Arya jumping towards the Night King

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.891
and stabbing him in the heart with

00:00:21.891 --> 00:00:24.070
a Valyrian steel dagger.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.792
Showrunners David Benioff and D.B. Weiss

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.000
claim that they have known for years

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.030
that she would be the one
to kill the Night King.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.770
But you might not have
spotted all the clues

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.520
that they put in other episodes.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.510
We're going to break it down for you.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.204
Right from the start in
season one, episode one,

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:39.730
Arya is introduced to us as a force

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.940
to be reckoned with,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.021
while her brother Bran is set up

00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:43.420
to not be a great warrior.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.270
Arya comes in with a sneak
attack and hits the target.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.620
Season one, episode two, Arya is bestowed

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.301
with her first weapon, Needle, by Jon.

00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:53.326
Jon's advice is:

00:00:53.326 --> 00:00:54.720
Stick 'em with the pointy end.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.543
Ju: This line is repeated
in "The Long Night."

00:00:57.543 --> 00:00:59.350
Stick 'em with the pointy end.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.420
Ju: Arya's teacher after
Jon was Syrio Forel,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.800
who taught her to be fast,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.937
coining the phrase,

00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:05.433
"What do we say to the god of Death?

00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:06.940
Not today,"

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.560
which again was repeated
in "The Long Night."

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.520
Ironically, in her first lesson with him,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.930
he throws a sword towards her,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.360
which she fails to catch.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.540
Tomorrow you will catch it.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.180
The Catspaw Dagger's journey through

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.680
the seasons is actually a clue in itself.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.551
It makes an early
appearance in season one.

00:01:21.551 --> 00:01:23.108
A mysterious assassin tries to murder

00:01:23.108 --> 00:01:25.750
Bran with it, but Catelyn
Stark protects him.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.190
So Catelyn takes it to King's Landing

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.560
where she shows it to Littlefinger.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.250
He frames Tyrion, which then turns

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.610
into the War of the Five Kings.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.443
Ned Stark has it,

00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:33.440
then loses it to Littlefinger

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.408
when he betrays him,

00:01:34.408 --> 00:01:35.531
leading to Ned Stark's death,

00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:37.122
which then sends Arya on her long journey

00:01:37.122 --> 00:01:38.397
to becoming a bada-- assassin,

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.460
only for Littlefinger to give it back

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.430
to Bran at the same location

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.633
it is first introduced.

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:43.220
This is for you.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.587
Ju: In season seven,
episode one, that exact

00:01:45.587 --> 00:01:47.492
dagger shows up in one of the books

00:01:47.492 --> 00:01:49.650
that Sam is reading in
the Citadel in Oldtown

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.900
to find out how to defeat
the army of the dead

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.457
and the Night King.

00:01:53.457 --> 00:01:56.587
Melisandre meets Arya in
season three, episode six,

00:01:56.587 --> 00:01:57.887
telling her:

00:01:57.887 --> 00:01:59.130
I see a darkness in you,

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.288
and in that darkness,
eyes staring back at me.

00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:14.765
Ju: This is the prompt
Melisandre uses again

00:02:14.765 --> 00:02:16.850
in season eight, episode three to send her

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.885
over to the weirwood tree.

00:02:19.885 --> 00:02:21.840
In season four, Arya picks up

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.530
a few tips from the Hound.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.856
In their travels across Westeros,

00:02:24.856 --> 00:02:27.620
he teaches her to look
for weak spots in armor

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.600
and also how to stab someone in the heart.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.332
In season six, episode
five, Bran has a vision

00:02:33.332 --> 00:02:35.467
where he experiences the
creation of the Night King

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.170
by the Children of the Forest.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.880
What we now know as the Night King

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.120
gets stabbed in the chest

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.048
by a dragonglass dagger.

00:02:42.048 --> 00:02:44.142
It's under a similar-looking weirwood tree

00:02:44.142 --> 00:02:45.560
that he would meet his demise,

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.450
again being pierced in the chest.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.020
In season eight, episode one,

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.920
Arya sneaks up on Jon Snow
in exactly the same place

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.650
where she kills the Night King.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.557
He says:

00:02:55.557 --> 00:02:57.540
How did you sneak up on me?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.600
In season seven, episode four,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.878
Bran gives Arya the dagger that he in turn

00:03:01.878 --> 00:03:03.830
was given by Littlefinger.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.410
The Littlefinger scene had seemed a

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.070
bit random at the time,
and he turns it over

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:08.920
to her, saying:

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:09.753
I don't want it.

00:03:09.753 --> 00:03:11.980
Ju: It's a testament to
Isaac William Hempstead's

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.204
portrayal of Bran that without realizing

00:03:14.204 --> 00:03:16.257
its significance, he has a wistful

00:03:16.257 --> 00:03:18.210
and kind of knowing look on his face,

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.519
as if giving the dagger some significance.

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:23.238
Once Bran gives the dagger to Arya,

00:03:23.238 --> 00:03:24.910
it's extremely visible on her belt

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.039
throughout the next episodes.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.640
She then used it in a sparring

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.139
match with Brienne, using the same

00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:32.763
drop move that she did
with the Night King.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.010
Characters die protecting Arya,

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:39.120
almost as if saving her
life is the main objective:

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.280
Ser Beric Dondarrion and Syrio Forel.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.480
Then we come to season
eight, episode three itself.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.610
The Hound has a seemingly
distracting breakdown

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.507
during the episode, saying to Ser Beric:

00:03:49.507 --> 00:03:52.416
We're fighting death.
They can't beat death.

00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:56.570
Ju: His reply is to point to
Arya and say, "Tell her that."

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.560
Arya also repeats moves during the episode

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.120
that we've seen her do in previous fights.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.980
Her first encounter with a wight mimics

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.077
her season-six training
with the Faceless Men,

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.896
stopping the staff in the same position.

00:04:07.896 --> 00:04:09.700
It should have been obvious that Arya was

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.570
being built up for something special.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:12.920
Throughout the show, she has gone through

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.100
a lot of training.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.720
It was never really
clear what this training

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.750
would be for other than
killing people on her list.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.280
We now know that it was to save the

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.100
Seven Kingdoms from its
most dangerous adversary.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.070
Did you spot any other
clues that we missed?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.993
Comment below.

